37:## States
43:| `local_lagging` | upstream published newer content that our copy lacks, **no longer than** `STALE_GRACE_HOURS` (30) ago: a cache served our fetcher an old copy, or the daily fetch ran before upstream published. `lag` = upstream `Date` minus upstream content clock (`pft_upstreamwatch_feed_lag_seconds`, LAG column). For `usn-host` the [bounded heal](#bounded-heal) refetches once the lag exceeds `LAG_HEAL_HOURS` | `PFTUpstreamFeedLagging`, `notify="digest"`, `for: 3h`, **never paged** |
50:(not latest: `local_lagging` while lag <= grace, `local_stale` after it). Before 2026-11-27 a lag within the grace
59:## Bounded heal
65:next fetch was a day away (live capture: `tests/fixtures/obs-live-validator-20261127.json`). `local_lagging` makes the
69:   `../vulnscan`) in `local_lagging` or `local_stale` with `lag > LAG_HEAL_HOURS`. In this order it then skips
70:   `disabled` (`LAG_HEAL_HOURS=0`), `rate_limited` (the last start for this feed was less than `HEAL_INTERVAL_HOURS`
82:   the next try is `HEAL_INTERVAL_HOURS` later) or `failed` (the unit start failed). The result is written to
86:JSON line (the last 1000 are kept) and printed to the unit's journal. At most `24 / HEAL_INTERVAL_HOURS` (4) refetches
92:| `LAG_HEAL_HOURS` | `2` | heal a feed whose lag is **more** than this; `0` = never heal |
93:| `HEAL_INTERVAL_HOURS` | `6` | at most one heal start per feed in this many hours (counted from the last start) |
